camera on the battle plot.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Strength Color Coding[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Effective strength columns are color-coded relative to the unit's max effective strength: white at full, green above 66%, yellow above 33%, red at 33% or below.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Sorting and Logging[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Click any column header to sort numerically/alphabetically.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]The LOG button (when enabled via SAS define) writes the visible battle history to PythonDbg.log for external inspection.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Blank Values[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Blank cells can mean the value is zero or not applicable (for example, the lost unit died, no worker was captured), or that the row was not recorded fully for some reason (early version of this feature, bug to fix, etc.).</English>
